{"abstract":[{"text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, extending through each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order to an unvisited vertex. Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"searches.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Tours"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE15hamiltonianPath5Walks0E0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Hamiltonian.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Hamiltonian.swift#L552"},"symbolKind":"method","title":"hamiltonianPath()","role":